Creating  a Stand involes maching the mechanical parts and attaching a stand ability

Creating mechanically
Choose a range for your stand to physically operate within. //The stands physical range is not neccesarily the stands ability range

  Close range	1-2 Meters:           +5 to Brawl and tough checks
  Long range	50 meters:            No Bonus
  Automatic	  Conditional:  	      +5 to Brawl and tough checks
  Zero Range	Within or on body:  	+10 to Brawl and tough checks

Then Apply Modifiers to your stand to make it more unique

  Good Looking:	                  Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when making a first impression.
  Pure of Heart:	                Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 3 when searching for a helpful ally.
  High Stand Potantial:	          Gain 2 Tokens when you fail a check.
  The Joestar Secret Technique:	  Lower the DC of any Check by 1 when Running Away.
  Flashy:	                        Lower the DC of a Hot Check by 5 if it’s the first roll after you’ve crit.
  Has a Drivers License:	        Lower the DC of a Tech Check by 3 if it involes driving.
  Inspiring:	                    Each time you succeed at a check, an ally of your choice receives 1 Token.
  Loyal:                        	Your Tokens give friends +1 at a one-to-one rate.
  Lucky:                        	Once Per Episode Spend 2 Tokens to reroll any check.
  Menacing:                      	Use Brawl instead of Hot when intimidating an NPC.
  Nerves of Steel:              	Spend a Token to treat a snap decision as a Prepared Action.
  Poker Face:                    	When attempting to conceal the truth, use Tough instead of Hot.
  Prepared:                      	Spend 2 Tokens to just happen to have one commonplace item with you.
  Protector:                    	Lower the DC of a check by 3 when defending your friends.
  Quick Healing:                	Recover one injury level at the end of an encounter.
  Resilient:                    	Turbo Tokens are worth double when used to boost against an attack that targets you.
  Skilled:                      	Increase your die type for one skill by 1 for the purposes of halving.
  Flashback:                    	Describe a pep talk you gave earlier to spend Turbo Tokens for a friend, even when you are not present.
  Stealthy:                       Lower the DC of a Sneak Check by 3 when trying to avoid being seen.
  Suspicious:                    	Lower the DC of a Wits Check by 3 when trying to determine if someone is lying to you.
  Grit:                          	Lower the DC of a Tough Check by 3 when resisting a Brawl Check.
  Your Next Line Is:              Spend a Turbo Token to force an enemy to resist your Brawl with Wits instead of Tough.
  Leap of Faith:                  Lower the DC of a Stunts Check by 3 when making a jump that could injure you.
  Hacker:                        	Lower the DC of a Tech Check by 3 when breaking into a computer database.
  So It’s The Same Kind of Stand:	Lower the DC of a Brawl Check by 3 against someone wielding the same type of stand.
  Interrogator:                 	Lower the DC of a Wits Check by 3 to draw information out of an opponent.
  Main Character:               	You are the main character.
  Trouble Maker:               	Spend a Turbo Token to locate and receive help from a criminal network.
  Wealthy:                      Spend a Turbo Token to ease a bad situation with cash.
  Fast Hands:                    When an opponent attacks you, if you are within range of it, and no other hostile creatures are near you, use Brawl instead of Tough. 
  Death Flag:                     Once per episode, Roll tough on someone else's behalf.
  Shine on:                       Once per episode, Lend a teamate a skill die.
  Famous:                         Roll HOT in response to the first attack of an encounter to dissuade an opponent.
  Cooled Off:                     Roll twice on the first roll after an injury.
  Gangstar:                       After criting twice in a row, double the amount of tokens you have.
  Mulitasking:                    You and your stand may both take actions provided the first is successful.
  Hot Stuff:                      Two succesful Hot checks auto-succeed on stealing from an npc.
  Get Jumped:                     In a scene where every player (minimum 3) uses a difrent skill, reduce your range to crit by 1.
  Together:                       Once per episode, you and another player roll the same skill and add the totals together.
  Jojo Pose:                      Once per episode, you may strike a pose and take two Tokens.
  Kono Powa:                      Beating an oponent by 10 or more means you deal an additional injury.
  The One:                        Once per episode, Treat a Nat 1 as a max die roll.
  Switch Tactics:                 Once per episode, Reroll a Faliure with a different skill.
  Pallet Swap:                    Once per Episode, Accept a Critical Faliure to gain half Tokens of the die value.
  Infiite Growth:                 On a Nat 20, Restart that skill track, now rolling an additional die and taking the better result.
  Battle Tendency:                On a Nat 20, Everybody else at the table graduates all of their lowest die type up by one.
  Requiem:                        On a Nat 20, Become the GM for 60 seconds.
